Model Room - the first workbench
Workstream-ID: modelroom-01
Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/ModelRoom/issues/1
Project: https://github.com/users/Zanark/projects/11
Status: DONE
Milestone: Locally usable static 3D inspection and Blender interchange
Dependencies: None

Purpose:
Build the user's Model Room: an original static site where an agent-authored
model can be rotated, inspected, refined and downloaded for Blender.
Keep the distinction between an external coding agent and a static website explicit.

Tasks:
- [x] Inspect empty repository and original modeling handbook/toolchain.
- [x] Research geometry, camera controls, color, resource ownership and interchange.
- [x] Author original identity, responsive workspace and procedural cardboard box.
- [x] Implement actual part hierarchy, four hinged flaps and live dimensions/color.
- [x] Implement orbit/pan/zoom, camera presets, wireframe, grid and studio lighting.
- [x] Implement local GLB inspection, model-only export, PNG and recipe downloads.
- [x] Implement local prompt/reference brief without pretending to run an AI.
- [x] Validate browser controls, export/roundtrip, error paths and production build.
- [x] Complete README, guides, research receipts, journal and source contracts.
- [x] Mirror this workstream to its real issue/Project, verify actual states.
- [x] Persist owned context, refresh mesh and leave verified local hosting available.

Acceptance criteria:
The local website displays real geometry and allows all-around camera inspection.
The box has separate walls/flaps, finite geometry, explicit meter scale and
meaningful live controls. GLB contains the object/materials/embedded textures,
not viewer infrastructure; reimport preserves shape and parts. Actual Blender
import is tested if an existing installation is available; otherwise disclose
that environmental limit separately from structural glTF qualification.
Brief saving produces a real downloadable request; reference-image bytes are
not uploaded or silently claimed as included. Bad imports preserve the model.
Static production artifact works at a subpath without a runtime CDN.
Local hosting is responsive and running at handoff. No public deployment.
Docs/TODO/context and actual issue/Project agree with verified evidence.

